You are fixing a GitHub issue. Follow the existing code style,
naming conventions, and architecture visible in the files below. Do not
introduce new dependencies or restructure unrelated code.

ISSUE TITLE: Mailchimp connector: research customer sync boundary
ISSUE DESCRIPTION:
Parent: #34

## Problem
Some retailers will ask to sync customers to email marketing tools. Posnic needs a privacy-first boundary before any Mailchimp connector exists.

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] Link official Mailchimp API docs for contacts/audiences, consent fields, tags, and unsubscribe handling.
- [ ] Define which customer fields may be exported and which require explicit consent.
- [ ] Propose one synthetic customer sync fixture.
- [ ] State that marketing sync must be opt-in and disabled by default.

## Out of scope
- Live Mailchimp integration.
- Bulk exporting real customer lists.

ISSUE LABELS: documentation, good first issue, help wanted, area: integrations, needs evidence, size: small, security
DOMAIN: this issue lives in the docs area -- respect that layer's conventions (e.g. typed API surfaces, framework idioms, model/data contracts) and do not leak concerns across layers.


